            "review_title": "Review at Bibing Snow Milk Bingsu",
            "review_text": "Kathy L\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam7 contributions\n0\nCold Desserts, Warm welcome\nMay 2016 • Solo\nFIrst of all, the interior inside is very cozy, I felt wery comfortable and at ease. Comfortable sofas, bookshelfs and e.t.c. \nFor a price 30-45k you can get a big jar of fuzzy fruity soda, not in a long slim glass, but actually, a plenty of drink.\nBingsu was wonderful. Fluffy flakes that only ever melt when you put them in your mouth, with thick mango slices and a scoop of creamy ice cream on top.\n\nLittle twist in this dessert took an absolute victory over me, once I reached the bottom of Bingsu and found myself chewing on chunks of actual heavy cheesecake.\n\nWould reccomend. Great place, great desserts, great price.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 17, 2016",
